  "note": "The model ignores absolute size on the layout canvas and shortens or stretches a diagonal staff, so every drawing is measured and scaled by the geometric mean of its blindfold-cloth head scale and its staff-length scale (the two must agree within 20%). The guide images (stick figure plus a gold bar of the right staff length and line) are what kept the proportions: runs without a guide drew heads 1.3-1.8x too large and staffs about 0.6x too short. Pose guides carry only joint angles; she is painted fully from the identity image. Added 2026-10-12 (animation audit, rounds 1 and 2): round 1 added dash1, dash2, brake, rise, backstep and settle so every travel segment had stepping drawings; round 2 (reviewer with a stepped clock found skating and one-cut staff swings) replaced the grounded stride drawings dash1, dash2 and backstep with real flight drawings (leap, glide, descend, hop1, hop2, land) and added in-between drawings (ready0-ready3, swing, sweepmid, guard2) so no staff end moves more than 180 canvas px and no head more than 90 px between consecutive drawings. They use layout-s15 and a guide scale of 0.95, were drawn from an approved neighbouring drawing, and the sources were stored lossless because the blindfold and staff detectors need exact white and gold pixels. The flight drawings are lifted off the ground by the config `audit.airborne` values. The stored inputs/ images are the exact guides submitted for the added drawings (make-pose-inputs.py reproduces them byte for byte).",
